{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Built and filed the repair-path experiment for the registered question. The cluster harness now runs a repair phase after the healed split state: it puts a node holding the current configuration in charge (transferring leadership if the healed leader is the stale node), disconnects the restarted node, commits ten further entries on that leader, takes a snapshot on it with TrailingLogs 0 so its log is compacted past the restarted node's position, reconnects the node and waits for it to install the snapshot, then samples the conflict index and the applied commands again. Local construction feedback is deterministic on the asserted operands across three runs: the snapshot install happens (last snapshot index 22 or 23), the restarted node's applied write becomes majority-write, its divergent minority-write disappears, the conflict index no longer exists in its log, and its reported configuration becomes {A,B,C,D,E}, while a node that stayed up to date keeps the minority write, which is the negative half of the answer.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"12a64c3fb3bc403f9a55aa626c4f81eb-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_stale_election_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"8001bad80a4d4ef0a840634644afdf63-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Extends the live-cluster harness with a repair phase for a new question: leadership is handed to a current-configuration node, the restarted node is disconnected while the leader commits ten entries and snapshots with TrailingLogs 0, then reconnected and sampled after the resulting snapshot install. The earlier phases, admission and events are unchanged; the earlier comparisons stay with their own receipts.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"TrailingLogs is set to 0 for the cluster so a manual snapshot actually compacts the leader's log.\\\",\n   \\\"A repair phase is added after the healed sample: choose a current-configuration leader, cut the restarted node off, commit ten entries, snapshot the leader, reconnect the node, wait up to 15s for it to install a snapshot, then sample the conflict index and applied commands.\\\",\n   \\\"A fifth event 'repaired' reports the repair leader, applies, snapshot index, error, whether the snapshot was installed on the restarted node, its applied writes and configuration afterwards, whether the conflict index entry is gone, and the applied writes across the cluster.\\\"],\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"s-dupskip\\\",\\\"s-confentry\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Real 5-node in-memory cluster in which node A is restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs after a committed configuration change newer than its snapshot, splits {A,C} from {B,D,E} so both sides commit at the same index and term, is healed, and is then repaired by forcing a snapshot install from a current-configuration leader while A is temporarily unreachable.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"All phases are produced through normal operations: bootstrap, election, committed applies, a user snapshot, AddVoter, graceful restart, transport partition and reconnection.\\\",\n    \\\"TrailingLogs is 0 for every node, so the leader's snapshot compacts its log beyond the disconnected node's position, which is the condition that makes the leader send a snapshot instead of entries.\\\",\n    \\\"The snapshot install is observed through the restarted node's own last-snapshot index and its applied commands; the leader and the other nodes are not modified by the harness during the repair phase.\\\",\n    \\\"The repair phase records rather than asserts which current-configuration node leads: leadership is transferred to B only if the healed leader is not a current-configuration node.\\\"],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No user Restore, no compaction without a lagging follower and no term-changing truncation is exercised; only the snapshot-install path is.\\\",\n    \\\"The scenario stops after the first repaired sample; C is not repaired in the same run.\\\",\n    \\\"No on-disk store or crash is exercised and no repository test was executed.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"cluster_ids\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\",\\\"initial_configuration\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\",\\\"added_voters\\\":\\\"D,E\\\",\\\"partition\\\":\\\"A,C | B,D,E\\\",\\\"conflict_index\\\":11,\\\"repair_applies\\\":10,\\\"trailing_logs\\\":0}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness builds five InmemTransports (A..E) in a full mesh with per-node InmemStore, InmemCommitTrackingStore and InmemSnapshotStore and Config with TrailingLogs 0, bootstraps {A,B,C} from A, starts A, B and C with MockFSM and Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true, waits for a leader, transfers leadership to A if needed, applies three commands, waits on a Barrier and takes a user snapshot on A. It starts D and E, adds each as voter, applies one further command and emits 'fixture'. It shuts A down, cuts {A,C} from {B,D,E}, reconnects A to C only, restarts A from the same stores and emits 'restart'. It waits for a leader in each partition, submits one Apply to each leader, reads both leaders' entries at the shared index and emits 'outcome'. It reconnects the full mesh, waits for one leader, applies one further entry, waits 300ms and emits 'healed' with payloads, terms, applied write lists and configurations. It then runs the repair phase: it selects a leader among B, D and E (transferring leadership to B if the healed leader is not one of them), cuts A from every other node, applies ten commands on that leader, takes a snapshot on it, reconnects A, waits up to 15s for A's last snapshot index to reach the leader's snapshot index, waits 300ms and emits 'repaired'. All nodes are shut down afterwards. Event order: fixture, restart, outcome, healed, repaired.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft recovery path: the leader's snapshot plus log compaction (removeOldLogs/compactLogs with TrailingLogs 0) and the follower's installSnapshot handling, which restores the FSM and replaces the log and configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_config_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_entry_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_reported_config_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\"},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"commit_covers_config_entry\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n    {\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_before_config_entry\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_installed_on_a\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The ordinary recovery path should engage once the stale node falls behind a compacted leader: the node installs a snapshot.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_fsm_applied_writes_after_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"majority-write\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"After the snapshot install the restarted node's applied state should match the current configuration's side.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_write_present_on_a_after_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The command only the minority side had accepted should no longer be in the restarted node's applied state.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_conflict_index_entry_missing\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The divergent entry at the conflict index should be gone from the restarted node's log after the install.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_config_ids_after_snapshot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"The installed snapshot also carries the committed configuration, so the stale view should be gone afterwards.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"repaired\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\\\"asserti